I've left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so calling `https://metadata.internal.example/...` would need an `aap:caps/http-client` import that this node isn't authorised to hold. The host would reject the component at link time. The fetch also couldn't affect the output, so dropping it changes nothing. If you need enrichment, add an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability to the node's `with` clause in the graph first.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        // `id` is a parser-computed digest, safe to use as a store key.
        // Keep only items the 'seen' store has no record of, preserving order.
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

